<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heraclius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 575–641 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heraclius was a Byzantine emperor of the early seventh century who fought a long war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>. After major Persian advances, he campaigned deep into Persian territory and won a decisive victory in 627, forcing peace. The exhausting war left the Sasanian Empire weakened shortly before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Arab conquests</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heraclius.jpg" alt="Heraclius" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heraclius_solidus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
